<title>USA: Home Properties Q1 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Home Properties Q1 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.Y. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>HOME PROPERTIES OF NEW YORK INC</p>
<p>(in thousands, except share and per share data - Unaudited)</p>
<p>							Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							     March 31</p>
<p>							1997	     1996</p>
<p>   Total revenues				13,842	  10,540</p>
<p>   Total expenses				12,001	   9,730</p>
<p> Net income before minority interest	1,841	     810</p>
<p> FFO(B)					     4,150	   2,749</p>
<p>Weighted average shares/interests</p>
<p>   outstanding(C)			     9,254.7	 6,612.8</p>
<p>Per share/unit:</p>
<p>    Net income					.20	     .12</p>
<p>    FFO(B)					    .45	     .42</p>
<p>NOTE: The :net income&quot; in the headline refers to the &quot;Net income before minority interest&quot; specified in the table.</p>
<p>(B) FFO is defined as net income (calculated in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles) before gains or losses on sales of investments and extraordinary items plus depreciation from real property.</p>
<p>(C) Includes common stock plus operating partnership units and Class A limited partnership interests in Home Properties of New York L.P. which can be converted into shares of common stock.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
